8. Sovereign Data Supply Chain and Cryptography

8.1 SovDSC

Raw observations factorize as
Y_t^{\text{raw}} = \mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{pub}} \oplus \mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{sov}},


where $\mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{pub}} \in \mathbb{R}^{d_1}$ carries aggregated ecological indicators and $\mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{sov}} \in \mathbb{R}^{d_2}$ carries micro-spatial species locations, ethnobotanical identifications, eDNA sequences, and TEK inputs. The transformation is
\mathcal{F}_{\text{SovDSC}}(Y_t^{\text{raw}}, \mathcal{G}_t^{\text{policy}}) = (\mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{pub}} + \eta_\varepsilon, \pi_{\text{ZKP}}(\mathcal{Y}_t^{\text{sov}})),


with $\eta_\varepsilon \sim \mathrm{Laplace}(0, \Delta S / \varepsilon)$ differential-privacy noise and $\pi_{\text{ZKP}}$ a non-interactive zero-knowledge proof.

8.2 Zero-knowledge verification and the oracle problem

Definition 8.1 (ZKP ecological verification). A proof $\pi_{\text{ZKP}}$ lets Agent 10 confirm $X_t^{(k)} \geq x_{\text{threshold}}$ without revealing coordinates, species identities, or raw values:
\mathrm{Verify}(\pi_{\text{ZKP}}, vk, x_{\text{threshold}}) = 1 \iff X_t^{(k)} \geq x_{\text{threshold}}.

Oracle-trust boundary. Definition 8.1 establishes that a committed value satisfies a threshold. It does not establish that the committed value reflects an accurate, unmanipulated sensor reading. In cryptographic terms, the ZKP layer solves the verification problem but not the oracle problem: the binding of physical state to committed value is outside the proof system. Candidate mitigations — multi-sensor attestation with hardware roots of trust, randomized spot-check ground truth, bonded challenger games — are listed in §14.2 and are not currently specified.

8.3 Cryptographic restoration ledger

Each epoch $k$ appends a block
B_k = \langle k, H(B_{k-1}), t, i, \mathrm{MerkleRoot}(b_t), a_t^*, \sigma_{\text{Gov}}, \sigma_{\text{Verif}}, H(Y_{t+1}) \rangle,


with $\sigma_{\text{Gov}}$ the signature of Agent 11 / territorial council and $\sigma_{\text{Verif}}$ the independent verification signature of Agent 10.

8.4 Smart-contract payment

Let $\Delta E_t = E(X_{t+\tau}) - E(X_t)$. Disbursement is
\mathcal{S}_{\text{pay}}(B_k, \ldots, B_{k+\tau}) = \begin{cases} \mu \cdot \Delta E_t, & \text{if } \mathrm{VerifyChain} = 1 \text{ and all } \sigma \text{ valid}, \\ 0, & \text{otherwise}. \end{cases}

Caveat 8.2 (Payment architecture). Verification-triggered payment risks disadvantaging communities bearing upfront costs. We recommend a three-tranche structure: 30% advance on FPIC-verified design, 40% on milestone ledger entries, 30% on independent verification.

