11. Spatial Spillover and Net Landscape Restoration Gain

11.1 Leaky-bucket spatial deforestation model (corrected)

Let $\rho(x,t) \geq 0$ denote deforestation pressure density. The evolution is
\frac{\partial \rho(x,t)}{\partial t} = \nabla \cdot (D(x) \nabla \rho) - v(x) \cdot \nabla \rho + S_{\text{ext}}(x,t) - \mathcal{P}_{\text{enforce}}(x, u(t)),


with $D$ the diffusion tensor, $v$ the drift, $S_{\text{ext}}$ macro-economic demand, and
\mathcal{P}_{\text{enforce}}(x, u(t)) = \zeta \cdot \|I(a(t))\|_W \cdot \mathbb{1}(x \in \Omega_{\text{rest}}).

Corrected leakage coupling. v5's leakage integral lacked an $E$-vulnerability factor, making its bound dimensionally inconsistent. v6 adds the factor:
\mathcal{L}_{\text{spillover}}(u, x) = \int_{\Omega_{\text{rest}}} \int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} \sigma(x_i, x_j) \cdot \mathcal{P}_{\text{enforce}}(x_i, u_i) \cdot [1 - G_t(x_j)] \cdot E(x_j) \, dx_j \, dx_i,


with $\sigma(x_i, x_j) = \sigma_0 e^{-\|x_i - x_j\|/d_{\text{decay}}}$.

11.2 Net landscape restoration gain

Over $\Omega = \Omega_{\text{rest}} \cup \Omega_{\text{risk}} \cup \Omega_{\text{intact}}$,
\mathcal{G}_{\text{net}}(t) = \int_0^t \left( \dot{R}_{\text{gross}}(\tau) - \dot{D}_{\text{base}}(\tau) - \mathcal{L}_{\text{spillover}}(u(\tau), x(\tau)) \right) d\tau,


so
\frac{d \mathcal{G}_{\text{net}}}{dt} = \int_{\Omega_{\text{rest}}} (f_0(E) + g(E) u) \, dA - \int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} \lambda_{\text{defor}}(x,t) E(x,t) \, dA - \mathcal{L}_{\text{spillover}}(u, x).

11.3 Net positive landscape equilibrium

Theorem 11.1 (Spillover-resilient restoration bound). Assume (i) $\int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} E(x,t) \, dA > 0$; (ii) $\lambda_{\text{defor}}$ is $E$-weighted-mean-integrable with
\bar{\lambda}_{\text{defor}} = \frac{\int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} \lambda_{\text{defor}}(x,t) E(x,t) \, dA}{\int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} E(x,t) \, dA};


(iii) the leakage satisfies
\mathcal{L}_{\text{spillover}} \leq \bar{\sigma} \cdot \bar{\mathcal{P}}_{\text{enforce}} \cdot \int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} E(x,t) \, dA


for domain-averaged $\bar{\sigma}$, $\bar{\mathcal{P}}_{\text{enforce}}$. Then $d\mathcal{G}_{\text{net}}/dt > 0$ if
\frac{\int_{\Omega_{\text{rest}}} (f_0(E) + g(E) u) \, dA}{\int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} E(x,t) \, dA} > \bar{\lambda}_{\text{defor}} + \bar{\sigma} \cdot \bar{\mathcal{P}}_{\text{enforce}}.

Proof. Combine $d\mathcal{G}_{\text{net}}/dt > 0$, assumption (ii) for the deforestation term, and assumption (iii) for the leakage term; divide by $\int_{\Omega_{\text{risk}}} E \, dA > 0$. ∎

Remark 11.2. v5's proof pulled $\bar{\lambda}_{\text{defor}}$ out of the integral without defining it as an $E$-weighted mean and bounded the leakage by a quantity whose integrand did not include $E$. v6 corrects both.

Corollary 11.3 (Policy implication). Restoration must be co-deployed with legal-territorial protection ($G_t = 1$) to suppress $\bar{\sigma}$ — motivating the coupling of $u_i \geq C_{\text{protection}}^{(i)} \mathbb{1}(G_t^{(i)} = 1)$ in §9.3 with the spatial protection term in §11.1.

