14. Validation, Falsifiability, and Open Problems

14.1 Structural falsifiers

The framework is rejected if controlled experiments show any of:

1. AERA is Pareto-dominated by a static baseline on $(E_T, \sum_t \gamma^t \|I(a_t)\|_W)$.
2. Drone LiDAR MAPE > 0.30.
3. Multi-agent consensus fails to terminate in > 5% of rounds under Algorithm 1 (v6).
4. The recursive CVaR-constrained policy has a higher failure rate than a CVaR-blind baseline.
5. Intervention intensity does not monotonically decrease in $R_t$.
6. Any unverified FPIC override appears on the ledger.
7. The measure-based slack of Corollary 6.8 is violated by more than $C_{\text{bd}} \varepsilon_L (1-\gamma^{T+1})/(1-\gamma)$ on field data.

14.2 Open problems

1. Non-concave MEROI. Global optimality of Theorem 9.3 fails without concavity; robust non-convex portfolio methods needed.
2. SPRT multiplicity. Alpha-spending designs must be formalized and pre-registered before Phase 1.
3. Canopy attenuation $\mu_{\text{canopy}}$. Nuisance parameter whose identification may be weak under persistent cloud cover; strategy must be pre-registered.
4. DAG validation. Parent structure $\mathrm{Pa}(\cdot)$ is a working hypothesis; conditional independence tests required.
5. ZKP scalability. Non-interactive ZKPs over ecological thresholds require succinct proof systems.
6. ZKP oracle problem. ZKPs prove properties of committed values, not correspondence to physical reality. Candidate mitigations: multi-sensor attestation, hardware roots of trust, bonded challenger games. None currently specified.
7. Governance Agent independence. Full multi-signature specification deferred.
8. Participatory weight elicitation. Empirical validation of inter-rater reliability, appeals resolution, and temporal stability required.
9. Assumption 6.6 (A-BOUNDARY). The boundary-layer mass bound must be verified against field data on $\partial \mathcal{X}_{\text{unsafe}}$.
10. Dynamical-parameter identification. Parameters $r, \alpha, \gamma, \eta, E_{\text{low}}, E_{\text{mature}}, g_0, \theta, \kappa, \phi$ must be estimated per parcel.
11. Spatial kernel estimation. $D(x)$, $v(x)$, $\sigma(x_i, x_j)$ must be estimated from remote-sensing and enforcement data; estimation error propagates into Theorem 11.1.
12. Verification of $\Delta E_t$ without revealing sovereign data. Verifiable computation or trusted-oracle designs needed.
13. Xie (2021) citation. The volume/page range should be confirmed against the print version before submission.
14. Recursive CVaR vs static trajectory CVaR gap. The gap between the constraint (A1) and the static diagnostic $\mathrm{CVaR}_\alpha^{\mathfrak{P}}$ is an open quantitative question.

