Appendix C — Governance Constraint Algebra

C.1 Proof of Theorem 4.6

Theorem C.1 (Restatement of Theorem 4.6). Under Definitions 4.1, 4.3, and 4.5, if consent is revoked at time $t_r$ for parcel $i^*$ and action $a^*$, then for all $t^+ \geq t_r$,
C_{\text{FPIC}}(a^*) = 0.

Proof. Since $\mathsf{T}(i^*) = 1$ is deterministic and time-invariant within a planning epoch, $i^* \in \mathcal{I}_{\text{ind}}$. By Definition 4.5, the tuple $(i^*, a^*, \cdot, \cdot)$ is removed from $\Theta_{t^+}^{\text{FPIC}}$ for all $t^+ \geq t_r$. The factor
\mathbb{1}[a^* \in \mathrm{ApprovedActions}(\Theta_{t^+}^{\text{FPIC}}, i^*)]


is zero because no tuple in $\Theta_{t^+}^{\text{FPIC}}$ authorizes $a^*$ on $i^*$. Since $C_{\text{FPIC}}$ is a product over $i \in \mathcal{I}_{\text{ind}}$, one zero factor makes the entire product zero. ∎

C.2 Proof of Corollary 4.7

Corollary C.2 (Restatement of Corollary 4.7). Suppose $\mathcal{A}_1(b_t) = \{a : C_{\text{FPIC}}(a) = 1, C_{\text{Hydro}}(a, b_t) \leq 0\} = \emptyset$. Then the lexicographic projection $\Pi_{\mathcal{L}_1}$ returns $a_{\text{passive}}$, which by Axiom 4.4 satisfies $C_{\text{FPIC}}(a_{\text{passive}}) = 1$ and $C_{\text{Hydro}}(a_{\text{passive}}, b_t) \leq 0$.

Proof. By definition, $\Pi_{\mathcal{L}_1}(\mathcal{A}_0) = \mathcal{A}_1$. When $\mathcal{A}_1 = \emptyset$, the operator is defined to return $a_{\text{passive}}$ (this is the completion of the definition of $\Pi_{\mathcal{L}_1}$). Axiom 4.4 guarantees $C_{\text{FPIC}}(a_{\text{passive}}) = 1$. Since $a_{\text{passive}}$ has $W_{\text{demand}} = 0$, we have $C_{\text{Hydro}}(a_{\text{passive}}, b_t) = -\mathbb{E}_{X \sim b_t}[W_t + \Delta W_{\text{recycle}}] \leq 0$ whenever $W_t \geq 0$ (which holds by definition of $W_t \in \mathcal{X}_W \subseteq [0, \infty)$). ∎

